WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.912
SPEED is tested broadly.

00:00:03.992 --> 00:00:07.903
On the standard side,

00:00:07.983 --> 00:00:11.895
it uses CIFAR-10 and CIFAR-100 at thirty-two by
thirty-two resolution and TinyImageNet at sixty-four by sixty-four.

00:00:11.975 --> 00:00:15.886
To stress high-resolution performance,

00:00:15.966 --> 00:00:19.878
it uses six ImageNet subsets at one-twenty-eight by
one-twenty-eight,

00:00:19.958 --> 00:00:23.869
each with ten classes: ImageNette, ImageWoof,
ImageFruit, ImageMeow, ImageSquawk,

00:00:23.949 --> 00:00:27.861
and ImageYellow.

00:00:27.941 --> 00:00:31.852
Robustness is measured on CIFAR-100-C with fourteen
corruption types at five severity levels.

00:00:31.932 --> 00:00:35.844
Everything is compared under equal storage budgets,
counted in parameters per class,

00:00:35.924 --> 00:00:39.835
at one, ten, and fifty images per class.

00:00:39.915 --> 00:00:43.827
The default backbone is a ConvNet,

00:00:43.907 --> 00:00:47.818
the default matching objective is trajectory matching,

00:00:47.898 --> 00:00:51.810
and generalization is checked on MLP, ResNet18, and ViT.
